Patch 7917 (experimental, rollback netcode): RSX-side writes into guest main memory are reported, and a read-only view of the FIFO walker.

libs/video notes every RSX-side store into guest MAIN memory (destination below 0xC0000000, so not local memory) through
ps3_rsx_note_write(ea, bytes, kind): the 2D engines' row stores (gcm_store, the scaled-image row loop, the inline and per-word 2D writes,
the tiled writes through rsx_tiling_put), the draw engine's surface and depth write-back to guest memory (linear and tiled), GET_REPORT
and NOTIFY into main memory (kind 0), and semaphore / label releases (kind 1: the 0x6C label method, the 0x1D70/0x1D74 release). The loops
notify once per row or word run, not per pixel. Not covered: the HLE semaphore injects at VM_HLE_INJECT_BASE.
ps3_gcm_walker_view(out) reads the drain passes, the walker's get offset, flips queued / reached / completed, the drain thread id, the 7
command words at get and the write counter, for the snapshot gate's failure line. ps3_rsx_guest_write_hook (NULL by default) lets the
rollback snapshot's write guard (installer/port/jsp/jsp_snapshot.cpp, only with JSP_ROLLBACK=1) test each write against its saved ranges.
No behaviour change. Always-on bookkeeping, which changes nothing the game does while the hook is NULL: one call, one address compare, one counter
increment and one NULL check of the hook per noted store, row or word run, and one counter increment per FIFO drain
pass. Applies after 7916.

